# Files that Prettier must not rewrite.
#
# `src/core/mutation-sinks.generated.ts` is written by `scripts/generate-mutation-sinks.mts` and
# regenerated whenever a tool's handler changes. Two problems with letting Prettier own it:
#
#   - `format:check` runs last in `npm run check`, so every regeneration made the full check fail on a
#     file nobody hand-edited. Measured, repeatedly. A check that cries wolf over generated output is a
#     check people learn to ignore, and the next real failure goes unread with it.
#   - Prettier and the generator would disagree about layout on every run, so regenerating produced a
#     diff even when no tool had changed.
#
# The generator still emits readable, stable output, and the drift test in
# `tests/security-boundaries.test.ts` is what keeps it honest - it compares the committed file against a
# fresh scan and fails when they differ. That is a stronger guarantee than a formatter gives, because it
# checks the content rather than the whitespace.
